WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.935
We followed Fritz as fast as possible.

2
00:00:15.935 --> 00:00:20.886
But no matter how quickly Jack and I paddled the canoe, we couldn't keep up with the kayak.

3
00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:24.775
"Faster!" cried Ernest. "We have to catch him!"

4
00:00:24.775 --> 00:00:29.751
We soon arrived outside Safety Bay and passed the rocks that had trapped the wreck.

5
00:00:29.751 --> 00:00:33.866
Although we looked in every direction, we saw no sign of Fritz.

6
00:00:33.866 --> 00:00:36.043
Then we heard a pistol shot.

7
00:00:36.043 --> 00:00:38.754
"Do you think that's Fritz?" asked Jack.

8
00:00:38.754 --> 00:00:42.810
I fired a shot, which was immediately answered by another shot.

9
00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:46.691
We steered in the direction of the sound and soon saw Fritz.

10
00:00:46.691 --> 00:00:53.436
His kayak darted from behind a point of land, and he paddled over to our canoe, relieved to see us.

11
00:00:53.436 --> 00:00:57.460
"I didn't intend to pass out of sight, Father," he apologized.

12
00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:01.487
"But once in the water, I was carried along and couldn't help myself.

13
00:01:01.487 --> 00:01:05.479
Then I saw some strange animals that I thought were walruses and—"

14
00:01:05.479 --> 00:01:09.524
"Walruses!" said Ernest. "I thought they lived in the Arctic."

15
00:01:09.524 --> 00:01:13.153
"I gave chase, but I couldn't catch them—whatever they were."

16
00:01:13.153 --> 00:01:16.822
"You're safe and that is what's important," I said.

17
00:01:16.822 --> 00:01:19.348
I wanted us to all travel together.

18
00:01:19.348 --> 00:01:23.201
But Fritz was eager to go ahead and announce our arrival to Mother.

19
00:01:23.201 --> 00:01:27.065
He was soon skimming over the water while we followed at a slower pace.

20
00:01:27.065 --> 00:01:30.506
Meanwhile black clouds were gathering above us.

21
00:01:30.506 --> 00:01:33.126
Fritz was out of sight and beyond our reach.

22
00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:39.248
We fastened on our life preservers and tied ourselves to the canoe so that we wouldn't be washed overboard.

23
00:01:39.248 --> 00:01:42.868
Fearful gusts of wind lashed the ocean into foam.

24
00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:46.622
Sheets of rain washed over us while lightning flashed.

25
00:01:46.622 --> 00:01:51.083
But the storm swept on its way, and it was over as quickly as it had begun.

26
00:01:51.083 --> 00:01:54.678
Both Ernest and Jack had faced the danger with great courage.

27
00:01:54.678 --> 00:01:56.823
I was proud of them.

28
00:01:56.823 --> 00:02:01.157
I had never lost hope for us, but I feared that Fritz had drowned.

29
00:02:01.157 --> 00:02:04.761
With a heavy heart, I paddled into Safety Bay.

30
00:02:04.761 --> 00:02:07.980
"Look! It's Fritz!" cried Jack.

31
00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:11.859
There on shore were Fritz, Mother, and little Franz.

32
00:02:11.859 --> 00:02:15.828
Kneeling in prayer, they did not notice us until we shouted.

33
00:02:15.828 --> 00:02:22.096
"You're safe!" cried Franz. He ran to greet us as we pulled the canoe onshore.

34
00:02:22.096 --> 00:02:26.375
"Yes," I said. "Everyone is safe and we are thankful for that."

35
00:02:26.375 --> 00:02:32.337
Returning joyfully to Rockburg, we exchanged our drenched garments for warm, dry clothes.

36
00:02:32.337 --> 00:02:35.915
Seated at a good meal, we talked about the storm.

37
00:02:35.915 --> 00:02:39.723
It was obvious that it had caused a lot of damage at Rockburg.

38
00:02:39.723 --> 00:02:44.081
The next day we discovered that the storm had partly destroyed our bridge.

39
00:02:44.081 --> 00:02:48.292
We were kept busy repairing that for quite some time.

40
00:02:48.292 --> 00:02:50.603
Then it was the fishing season again.

41
00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:56.876
Our storage room was soon stocked with large quantities of herring and sturgeon.

42
00:02:56.876 --> 00:03:01.820
Many quiet days passed after that, and I noticed that my sons were bored.

43
00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:06.370
Fritz proposed that the boys go away for a few days on an expedition.

44
00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:10.583
Ernest, as usual, preferred to remain with my wife and me.

45
00:03:10.583 --> 00:03:15.686
Just as they were ready to start, I noticed Jack slipping some pigeons into a basket.

46
00:03:15.686 --> 00:03:19.221
Then he hid the basket under some packages in the cart.

47
00:03:19.221 --> 00:03:25.327
"Jack is probably afraid the boys won't find anything to eat on their expedition," I said to my wife.

48
00:03:25.327 --> 00:03:30.884
She smiled. "He might prefer to go hungry rather than eat a tough, old pigeon."

49
00:03:30.884 --> 00:03:33.958
The three boys started off in high spirits.

50
00:03:33.958 --> 00:03:42.444
Storm and Grumble pulled the cart as usual, ridden by Fritz and little Franz, while Jack dashed ahead on Hurry the ostrich.

51
00:03:42.444 --> 00:03:47.415
That evening we sat on the porch at Rockburg, wondering what the boys were doing.

52
00:03:47.415 --> 00:03:52.365
"We might have news of them soon," said Ernest, looking rather mysterious.

53
00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:55.522
Just then a pigeon landed on the porch railing.

54
00:03:55.522 --> 00:03:58.798
"What is that tied to its leg?" asked my wife.

55
00:03:58.798 --> 00:04:02.669
Ernest went over to the pigeon and brought back a scrap of paper.

56
00:04:02.669 --> 00:04:06.820
"It's the very latest news," he said, handing me the note.

57
00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:10.839
Dear Parents and Ernest, We have reached Woodlands.

58
00:04:10.839 --> 00:04:14.712
At Wood Lake we captured three young black swans.

59
00:04:14.712 --> 00:04:17.466
Won't they look fine floating on Safety Bay?

60
00:04:17.466 --> 00:04:20.079
Love to all. Fritz

61
00:04:20.079 --> 00:04:23.133
The next morning we sent a message back with the pigeon.

62
00:04:23.133 --> 00:04:28.048
And every evening we received another message describing that day's adventures.

63
00:04:28.048 --> 00:04:34.645
Usually Fritz wrote about the animals they saw, but one night his message was truly alarming.

64
00:04:34.645 --> 00:04:38.500
Dear Parents and Ernest, Today we visited the Gap.

65
00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.879
The bamboo fence has been completely broken down!

66
00:04:41.879 --> 00:04:46.014
The fields have been trampled, and we've seen huge footprints.

67
00:04:46.014 --> 00:04:47.721
Come to us, Father.

68
00:04:47.721 --> 00:04:52.167
We are safe right now, but feel we are no match for this unknown danger.

69
00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:55.960
Fritz
